        "en-US": "Master Sarará's journey in capoeira began in August 1977, at the SESC in the Setor Universitário, in Goiânia. Under the guidance of Master Passarinho, he trained alongside names that would become major references, such as Master Suíno and Master Ilustre. Sarará, who initially reached the yellow-scarf graduation, witnessed and took part in the evolution of the graduation system, which adopted the colors of the flag of Brazil. In 1990, Master Suíno graduated his first masters, including Sarará, who from then on took on the nickname that stays with him to this day. In 1999, he established important work in Cáceres-MT, collaborating with social programs and educational institutions. In an enriching experience, Master Sarará lived in Europe for two years starting in 2004, leaving a legacy of work and knowledge in Spanish cities such as Bilbao, Vitoria, and Valencia. Back in Brazil in 2006, he consolidated projects in Argentina (Córdoba), Trindade, and Goiânia, including partnerships with the Military Police and the Art and Education Project. In the years that followed, Master Sarará devoted himself to teaching training courses and organizing events for his students in various cities across Goiás, São Paulo, and Mato Grosso, consolidating his influence in national capoeira. In 2018, he was in Rondonópolis, returning to Cáceres in 2019, keeping his passion and work active.",
